WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:03.736
-The president appointed
Mike Pence to take charge

00:00:03.736 --> 00:00:05.404
of the response to
the coronavirus

00:00:05.404 --> 00:00:08.241
and held a press conference to
try to reassure Americans

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:10.810
that ended up reassuring
absolutely nobody.

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:13.279
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:17.250 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:20.085
-Nearly 3,000 people worldwide
have died so far

00:00:20.085 --> 00:00:23.055
from the coronavirus,
and now the CDC has confirmed

00:00:23.055 --> 00:00:25.858
the first case here in the U.S.
of unknown origin.

00:00:25.858 --> 00:00:28.795
The stock market has plummeted
this week on fears of potential

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:31.597
global pandemic and officials
here are warning

00:00:31.597 --> 00:00:33.833
that a wider spread in
the U.S. is inevitable,

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:36.268
or as the president put it
during a press conference

00:00:36.268 --> 00:00:37.737
in India on Tuesday --

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:43.275
-You may ask about the
coronavirus, which is, you know,

00:00:43.275 --> 00:00:45.845
very well under control
in our country.

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:50.949
We have very few people with it
and the people that have it

00:00:50.949 --> 00:00:54.921
are -- in all cases I have not
heard anything other.

00:00:54.921 --> 00:00:57.457
Maybe there's something new
'cause for two days,

00:00:57.457 --> 00:00:59.692
I haven't been seeing too much
of that news of --

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:01.060
very much news.

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:05.064
-Man, that -- that trip to India
really screwed you up.

00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:06.999
[ Laughter ]
"You know, the problem is

00:01:06.999 --> 00:01:09.535
I'm still on India time, which
is ten hours ahead.

00:01:09.535 --> 00:01:11.637
So a lot of this stuff that's
happening in the States

00:01:11.637 --> 00:01:13.572
hasn't happened for me yet
because,

00:01:13.572 --> 00:01:16.175
you know, because
I'm in the future."

00:01:16.175 --> 00:01:17.343
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:18.844
Like, three weeks ago
you were literally

00:01:18.844 --> 00:01:21.281
going around D.C. holding up
newspapers to brag

00:01:21.281 --> 00:01:22.515
about your impeachment acquittal

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:24.050
like an extra from "Newsies."

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:27.553
Did you not think to at least
try reading one of them?

00:01:27.553 --> 00:01:31.257
"Look, we did it, coronavirus?"

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:32.525
Now, it turns out
Trump's statement

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:34.059
was only partially true.
It turns out

00:01:34.059 --> 00:01:35.627
he was watching the news,

00:01:35.627 --> 00:01:37.429
but only because he was
freaked out about the effect

00:01:37.429 --> 00:01:39.766
the virus was having
on the stock market,

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:41.567
and thus his political fortunes.

00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:43.703
-Our reporting indicates that
while he was in India,

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:46.272
he was watching the stock market
reaction very closely.

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:48.908
He was very nervous and upset

00:01:48.908 --> 00:01:50.743
to see what was happening
with the stock market.

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:53.146
He seemed to be more aware of
what was happening

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:55.614
with the stock market than
was actually happening

00:01:55.614 --> 00:01:57.850
with developments
with the virus.

00:01:57.850 --> 00:01:59.419
-Of course, he was.
That's the only thing

00:01:59.419 --> 00:02:00.920
Trump cares about,
the stock market.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:02.689
For one thing, it's very
easy to understand.

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:04.023
There's no reading involved.

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:05.859
All you have to do is look at
the little arrow

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:08.094
on the bottom corner of your TV,

00:02:08.094 --> 00:02:09.395
and see whether
it's red or green.

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:11.597
In fact, whoever controls
that thing could possibly

00:02:11.597 --> 00:02:14.900
drive Trump insane by flipping
it back and forth really fast.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:16.235
"Oh, that's good.

00:02:16.235 --> 00:02:18.037
Oh, no, that's bad.

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:20.205
Good. Bad.

00:02:20.205 --> 00:02:22.809
Good! Bad.

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:25.645
Oh, no.
Oh, somebody make it stop."

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:27.814
[ Laughter ]
There are only two reasons

00:02:27.814 --> 00:02:29.748
Trump only cares about
the stock market,

00:02:29.748 --> 00:02:32.518
one, it mostly benefits the
wealthy elite that he caters to,

00:02:32.518 --> 00:02:35.154
and two, he thinks it's crucial
to his re-election chances.

00:02:35.154 --> 00:02:37.456
"Politico" reported that
the White House is afraid

00:02:37.456 --> 00:02:40.126
the coronavirus could shape
Trump's 2020 fortunes.

00:02:40.126 --> 00:02:42.661
That's why Trump has been
spreading misinformation

00:02:42.661 --> 00:02:44.363
about the situation
and seemingly

00:02:44.363 --> 00:02:46.265
trying to just will
the problem away.

00:02:46.265 --> 00:02:48.100
For example, Trump
keeps comparing

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.569
coronavirus to the flu.

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:53.072
Now, coronavirus has a fatality
ratio about 20 times higher

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:55.441
than the flu and yet, when
an actual medical doctor,

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:57.910
CNN's Sanjay Gupta asked Trump
about that difference

00:02:57.910 --> 00:02:59.278
at his press conference
yesterday,

00:02:59.278 --> 00:03:01.414
Trump insisted that
Gupta was wrong.

00:03:01.414 --> 00:03:05.384
-You talked about the flu in
comparison to the coronavirus.

00:03:05.384 --> 00:03:08.087
Flu has a fatality ratio
of about .1%.

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:09.221
-Correct.

00:03:09.221 --> 00:03:10.590
-This has a fatality ratio

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:13.058
somewhere between 2% and 3%.

00:03:13.058 --> 00:03:14.827
-Well, we think.
We think.

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:16.896
We don't know exactly numbers.
-The numbers so far --

00:03:16.896 --> 00:03:18.130
-And the flu is higher
than that.

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:19.599
The flu is much
higher than that.

00:03:19.599 --> 00:03:21.867
[ Laughter ]
-He's -- He's a doctor.

00:03:21.867 --> 00:03:23.836
Why do you think you know
more than he does?

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:27.006
Do you do this during your
actual doctors' appointments?

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:30.209
"Mr. President, it looks like
you have an undigested hamburger

00:03:30.209 --> 00:03:31.444
lodged in your stomach."

00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:33.846
"No, you're wrong, that's
just my second heart."

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:35.881
[ Laughter ]
Trump probably thinks

00:03:35.881 --> 00:03:38.517
he knows more about actual
doctors because this guy

00:03:38.517 --> 00:03:39.819
was his actual doctor.

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:40.820
Do you remember him?

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.388
The guy who looks
less like a doctor

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:44.724
and more like he's hiding in the
witness protection program.

00:03:44.724 --> 00:03:47.193
[ Laughter ]
The guy whose fallback job

00:03:47.193 --> 00:03:49.094
is roadie for
Hootie and the Blowfish.

00:03:49.094 --> 00:03:51.096
[ Laughter ]
Trump probably did know more

00:03:51.096 --> 00:03:52.798
than this guy.
"Bad news, man,

00:03:52.798 --> 00:03:55.768
looks like you got your feet
where your brain should be."

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:57.136
[ Laughter ]
"No, I think you just

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:59.272
have it upside down."
"Oh, hey!

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:01.174
I guess you're right, man.
All right.

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:04.077
Want some medicine?"
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.077 --> 00:04:06.379
Now, look, it's important to be
cautious and not to panic,

00:04:06.379 --> 00:04:08.614
but it's also important
not to ignore

00:04:08.614 --> 00:04:10.249
the advice of health
professionals.

00:04:10.249 --> 00:04:12.351
Everyone should remain calm,
hope for the best,

00:04:12.351 --> 00:04:14.620
but follow the advice of experts
and be prepared.

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:17.089
For example, public health
officials have been warning

00:04:17.089 --> 00:04:18.992
this week that it's
not a matter of if,

00:04:18.992 --> 00:04:20.759
but when the virus spreads here.

00:04:20.759 --> 00:04:23.262
A top CDC official, the director
of the National Center

00:04:23.262 --> 00:04:26.198
for Immunization and Respiratory
Diseases said this week

00:04:26.198 --> 00:04:28.100
it was inevitable
and that disruption

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:29.835
to everyday life may be severe.

00:04:29.835 --> 00:04:31.771
So you can either believe
that expert,

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:34.373
a doctor and scientist who's
received numerous awards

00:04:34.373 --> 00:04:35.774
and worked in public health
for decades,

00:04:35.774 --> 00:04:37.777
or you can believe this expert.

00:04:37.777 --> 00:04:40.779
-The virus -- they're
working hard.

00:04:40.779 --> 00:04:42.848
Looks like by April,
you know, in theory,

00:04:42.848 --> 00:04:45.818
when it gets a little warmer,
it miraculously goes away.

00:04:45.818 --> 00:04:47.052
I hope that's true.

00:04:47.052 --> 00:04:48.554
[ Laughter ]
-What?

00:04:48.554 --> 00:04:50.990
[ Laughter ]
What are you talking about?

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:54.159
It will go away
when it gets warmer?

00:04:54.159 --> 00:04:57.430
We're talking about a possible
pandemic, not winter skin.

00:04:57.430 --> 00:05:00.566
[ Laughter ]
Also, no one ever says,

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:03.803
"In theory" followed by
the word, "miraculously."

00:05:03.803 --> 00:05:06.505
That just proves how bad
your theory is.

00:05:06.505 --> 00:05:08.641
"In theory, she'll catch me
having an affair

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:12.911
and it will miraculously make
our marriage stronger."

00:05:12.911 --> 00:05:14.781
But this isn't just a story
about Trump's incompetence,

00:05:14.781 --> 00:05:16.615
it's also a story about
Trump's priorities

00:05:16.615 --> 00:05:19.452
because while he's been doling
out trillions in tax cuts

00:05:19.452 --> 00:05:22.088
to corporations and the wealthy,
he's also been proposing

00:05:22.088 --> 00:05:24.423
massive cuts to health agency
spending,

00:05:24.423 --> 00:05:26.158
and when he was asked
about that yesterday,

00:05:26.158 --> 00:05:29.395
he just shrugged it off and said
he could rehire doctors

00:05:29.395 --> 00:05:30.529
whenever he wants.

00:05:30.529 --> 00:05:32.865
-Trump consistently called
for enormous cuts

00:05:32.865 --> 00:05:35.233
to the CDC and the N.I.H.
and the W.H.O.

00:05:35.233 --> 00:05:37.536
You talked a lot today about
how these professionals

00:05:37.536 --> 00:05:39.939
are excellent, highly critical
and necessary.

00:05:39.939 --> 00:05:41.907
Does this experience at all give
you pause about those --

00:05:41.907 --> 00:05:45.277
-No, because we can get money
and we can increase staff.

00:05:45.277 --> 00:05:47.313
We know all the people.
We know all the good people.

00:05:47.313 --> 00:05:49.649
If we have a need, we can
get them very quickly.

00:05:49.649 --> 00:05:51.884
When we need them, we can get
them back very quickly.

00:05:51.884 --> 00:05:54.219
-No, you can't.
You can't just fire

00:05:54.219 --> 00:05:56.555
a bunch of doctors and then hire
them back immediately

00:05:56.555 --> 00:05:57.956
when there's an emergency.

00:05:57.956 --> 00:06:01.294
You can't even get ahold of
a doctor after 2:45 on a Friday.

00:06:01.294 --> 00:06:02.995
[ Laughter ]
This situation

00:06:02.995 --> 00:06:04.864
should give Trump pause
about his health cuts

00:06:04.864 --> 00:06:07.467
but, of course, it won't because
nothing ever gives him pause.

00:06:07.467 --> 00:06:10.236
He literally doesn't even
pause between words,

00:06:10.236 --> 00:06:12.738
that's why he's constantly
sucking in air.

00:06:12.738 --> 00:06:16.075
[ Breaths ]

00:06:16.075 --> 00:06:18.511
[ Laughter ]
By the way, if you see someone

00:06:18.511 --> 00:06:20.546
sniffing like that on
the subway this week,

00:06:20.546 --> 00:06:23.382
move to the other end
of the car.

00:06:23.382 --> 00:06:25.617
In fact, Trump's team is so
deeply unprepared

00:06:25.617 --> 00:06:27.920
that even the Republican
Senators are getting frustrated

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:30.322
with their lack of basic
knowledge about the virus

00:06:30.322 --> 00:06:32.691
they're dealing with.
Louisiana Senator John Kennedy

00:06:32.691 --> 00:06:35.727
grilled the acting Secretary of
Homeland Security this week

00:06:35.727 --> 00:06:37.997
for some basic facts about
the spread of the disease,

00:06:37.997 --> 00:06:40.266
like how many cases the
department is expecting,

00:06:40.266 --> 00:06:42.167
and it only went
downhill from there.

00:06:42.167 --> 00:06:43.736
-Is someone modeling that?

00:06:43.736 --> 00:06:45.438
Do you have any way of guessing?

00:06:45.438 --> 00:06:47.606
-Again, H.H.S., through their
medical professionals are --

00:06:47.606 --> 00:06:48.841
-Yes, but you're head of

00:06:48.841 --> 00:06:50.142
Homeland Security.
-Yes, sir.

00:06:50.142 --> 00:06:51.777
-And your job is
to keep us safe.

00:06:51.777 --> 00:06:54.580
-Yes, sir.
-Do you know today how many

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:57.382
the experts are predicting --

00:06:57.382 --> 00:07:00.052
-We only know that, again,

00:07:00.052 --> 00:07:02.455
we anticipate those numbers
to grow in the U.S.

00:07:02.455 --> 00:07:06.525
-But, you can't tell us how many
your models are anticipating?

00:07:06.525 --> 00:07:08.494
-No, Senator.

00:07:08.494 --> 00:07:09.729
Again, I would defer you

00:07:09.729 --> 00:07:11.597
to the Health and Human
Services for that.

00:07:11.597 --> 00:07:12.731
-Okay.
-CDC.

00:07:12.731 --> 00:07:13.965
-Don't you think you ought
to check on that?

00:07:13.965 --> 00:07:15.000
You're the secretary.

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:16.702
I think you ought to
know that answer.

00:07:16.702 --> 00:07:19.305
-I understand that.

00:07:19.305 --> 00:07:23.342
-How is the coronavirus
transmitted?

00:07:23.342 --> 00:07:27.580
-Through a variety of ways,
obviously, human-to-human.

00:07:27.580 --> 00:07:29.415
-How is it transmitted?

00:07:29.415 --> 00:07:31.149
-A variety of different ways,
Senator.

00:07:31.149 --> 00:07:32.151
-Tell me what they are, please.

00:07:32.151 --> 00:07:33.519
-Again, human-to-human.

00:07:33.519 --> 00:07:35.654
-Oh, is that how
it's transmitted,

00:07:35.654 --> 00:07:37.690
from human to human?

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:40.526
"Sir, we believe coronavirus
is either transmitted

00:07:40.526 --> 00:07:42.994
from human to human
or by drinking

00:07:42.994 --> 00:07:44.597
a delicious Mexican beer.

00:07:44.597 --> 00:07:50.269
But we do think you can stop it
by putting a lime in the neck."

00:07:50.269 --> 00:07:52.738
Seriously, how can you be the
Secretary of Homeland Security

00:07:52.738 --> 00:07:54.473
and not know how many cases
you're expecting

00:07:54.473 --> 00:07:56.375
or how the disease
is transmitted?

00:07:56.375 --> 00:07:58.510
The better question would be,
what do you know?

00:07:58.510 --> 00:08:01.513
"We don't have a vaccine yet,
but what we can do is air drop

00:08:01.513 --> 00:08:04.082
calendars into every city in
America so they can count

00:08:04.082 --> 00:08:06.285
the days until April when the
disease will miraculously

00:08:06.285 --> 00:08:07.386
go away, in theory.

00:08:07.386 --> 00:08:09.021
In theory."
[ Laughter ]

00:08:09.021 --> 00:08:14.026
[ Applause ]
So, obviously, obviously,

00:08:14.026 --> 00:08:16.328
none of this is reassuring.

00:08:16.328 --> 00:08:19.966
Now, when he was whipping up a
panic about Ebola in 2014,

00:08:19.966 --> 00:08:22.668
Trump criticized then President
Obama's choice for a Czar,

00:08:22.668 --> 00:08:25.671
to lead the response, tweeting,
"Obama just appointed

00:08:25.671 --> 00:08:27.472
an Ebola Czar with zero
experience

00:08:27.472 --> 00:08:29.775
in the medical area
and zero experience

00:08:29.775 --> 00:08:32.144
in infectious disease control.
A total joke."

00:08:32.144 --> 00:08:34.613
So, to calm fears over the
spread of coronavirus yesterday,

00:08:34.613 --> 00:08:36.816
Trump announced that he was
taking his own advice

00:08:36.816 --> 00:08:39.751
and appointing a Czar with
in-depth medical experience.

00:08:39.751 --> 00:08:44.123
-I'm going to be announcing,
exactly right now,

00:08:44.123 --> 00:08:46.291
that I'm going to be putting
our vice president,

00:08:46.291 --> 00:08:47.726
Mike Pence, in charge.

00:08:47.726 --> 00:08:50.128
-Mike Pence?
[ Laughter ]

00:08:50.128 --> 00:08:52.598
What medical experience
does Mike Pence have?

00:08:52.598 --> 00:08:55.667
At best, he looks like a CPR
doll that won't let you do

00:08:55.667 --> 00:08:58.537
mouth to mouth on it.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:58.537 --> 00:09:01.506
[ Applause ]
Although --

00:09:01.506 --> 00:09:04.577
Although I guess it makes sense
he's in charge of diseases now

00:09:04.577 --> 00:09:06.812
because he always has an
expression that looks

00:09:06.812 --> 00:09:09.282
like number six
on the pain chart.

00:09:09.282 --> 00:09:12.018
Now, Trump explained
his appointment

00:09:12.018 --> 00:09:14.753
by claiming Pence had handled
health care in Indiana well,

00:09:14.753 --> 00:09:17.889
but in reality, he infamously
oversaw a totally preventable

00:09:17.889 --> 00:09:19.992
HIV outbreak in his home state.

00:09:19.992 --> 00:09:22.027
Trump should have picked someone
with relevant experience

00:09:22.027 --> 00:09:23.495
and a proven track record,
but instead,

00:09:23.495 --> 00:09:24.964
he picked a political
"yes man"

00:09:24.964 --> 00:09:27.132
because he doesn't have anyone
else left in his White House.

00:09:27.132 --> 00:09:29.868
I mean, Ben Carson
is an actual doctor,

00:09:29.868 --> 00:09:32.237
but even he is less well known
for his medical career

00:09:32.237 --> 00:09:34.940
at this point than he is for
realizing mid-interview

00:09:34.940 --> 00:09:36.675
that he left his luggage
in the car.

00:09:36.675 --> 00:09:38.978
-We just saw Mr. Trump here.
I asked him how did it go

00:09:38.978 --> 00:09:41.514
and he said great, and he said
he learned a lot of things.

00:09:41.514 --> 00:09:43.315
What do you think he took away
from today?

00:09:43.315 --> 00:09:44.950
-Oh, my luggage.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:48.120
Hold on.
-Okay.

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:50.956
-"We have good news to report on
the coronavirus.

00:09:50.956 --> 00:09:52.658
Oh, no.

00:09:52.658 --> 00:09:54.960
Oh, I left the vaccine
in the car."

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:58.063
[ Laughter ]
It's exactly the kind of

00:09:58.063 --> 00:10:00.166
situation when you want someone
competent in charge

00:10:00.166 --> 00:10:02.501
of the government who fills
the civil service

00:10:02.501 --> 00:10:04.236
with apolitical experts
and listens to them.

00:10:04.236 --> 00:10:06.505
Instead, we have a mentally
incompetent game show host

00:10:06.505 --> 00:10:07.706
who's incapable
of thinking about

00:10:07.706 --> 00:10:09.374
anything other than his own
self-interests.

00:10:09.374 --> 00:10:11.777
In the meantime, we have
to trust and listen

00:10:11.777 --> 00:10:14.413
to the hardworking apolitical
public health officials

00:10:14.413 --> 00:10:15.948
and as for the Trump
administration,

00:10:15.948 --> 00:10:16.848
just hope that it --

